      "problem": "Which of the following differential equations is a logistic growth equation?",
      "worked_solution": "A logistic growth equation has the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dt}=ky(a-y),\n$$\n\nwhere $k>0$ is a constant of proportionality, and $a>y$ is the carrying capacity.\n\nFrom the given options, the only logistic growth equation is\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dt}=40y(370-y).\n$$\n\nIn this case, the constant of proportionality is $k=40,$ and the carrying capacity is $a=370.$",
